IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ha-housing`

-- Housing Act 1980 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask about help from the Housing Authority, with the seat
-- and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act is constitutive: almost every operative provision is a power of the Authority, and the baseline
-- (ha-housing.l4) asks "does the Act let the Authority do this for me?" from one seat with two faces. Here three people
-- ask:
--   - the person buying or building a home with the Authority's help (a Part IV loan, a Division 4 purchase, or a loan
--     from another lender with a s 46 guarantee or s 47 subsidy): the buyer's half of the baseline's seat;
--   - the person who rents, or wants to rent, a home from the Authority (ss 28, 30, 31, 60, 68): the tenant's half;
--   - a lending institution lending to a home buyer, whose loan the Authority may guarantee (s 46) or whose interest it
--     may subsidise (s 47, "payments ... to approved lending institutions").
-- The Housing Authority and the Minister are never seats: their powers appear as what they mean for the person asking.
-- "Must the Housing Authority deal with my application" (s 15) is the same for the buyer and the tenant: one question,
-- a branch for each.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when the
-- situation does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the
-- same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. There are two:
--   - `how I am buying` (`How I am buying`), for the buyer: with a Part IV loan from the Authority; buying a house or land
--     from the Authority itself (Part III Division 4); with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender. The Act ties
--     the Minister's loan limit (s 40) and the mortgage (s 41) to a Part IV loan; the rent credit (s 31), the terms of
--     sale (ss 32-33) and the price limit (s 34) to a Division 4 sale; the gazetted rate (ss 33(6), 42(3)), more time
--     to pay (s 68, "moneys payable to the Authority") and duty and fees added to the debt (ss 72-73) to either; and the
--     guarantee (s 46, borrowing the Authority does not lend) and the interest subsidy (s 47, loans "made to them by
--     approved lending institutions") to a loan from another lender.
--   - `I rent a home from the Housing Authority now` (BOOLEAN), for the tenant: the rent (s 30) and more time to pay
--     rent (s 68) arise only for a tenant. FALSE: does not arise.
-- Whether the Authority can lend for a purpose (ss 35-38), what the Act decides about a lender, whether it can rent or
-- provide specialised housing (ss 28, 60), and a former tenant's rent credit asked by the tenant (s 31), arise in every
-- situation of their role and take no situation input. The lender has none.
--
-- The rules are in ha-housing.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the buyer and the tenant each answer is
-- the baseline export's own answer, wrapped. Where the situation settles a baseline input (a Division 4 purchase for s
-- 31(1); a Division 4 sale or Part IV loan for s 72), the layer passes it as TRUE instead of asking it again. No exported
-- question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Housing Act 1980 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help`
    `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority`
    `I am a bank or other institution lending to a home buyer`

DECLARE `How I am buying` IS ONE OF
    `with a loan from the Housing Authority (Part IV)`
    `buying a house or land from the Housing Authority itself (Part III Division 4)`
    `with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Rate` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `percent a year` HAS `the percentage` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Text answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the text` IS A STRING

DECLARE `Terms answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the terms` IS A `Terms of sale`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The situation helpers list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes
-- the OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was not read).
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I am buying`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is not a Part IV loan` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `with a loan from the Housing Authority (Part IV)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `buying a house or land from the Housing Authority itself (Part III Division 4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `how` IS A `How I am buying`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is not a Division 4 purchase` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `with a loan from the Housing Authority (Part IV)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying a house or land from the Housing Authority itself (Part III Division 4)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `how` IS A `How I am buying`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I owe the Authority nothing for it` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `with a loan from the Housing Authority (Part IV)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `buying a house or land from the Housing Authority itself (Part III Division 4)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `how` IS A `How I am buying`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is not a loan from another lender` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `with a loan from the Housing Authority (Part IV)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying a house or land from the Housing Authority itself (Part III Division 4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender` THEN FALSE

-- The lender's facts about its borrower, put into the baseline's record.
GIVEN `eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a home` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Applicant
`the borrower as an applicant` `eligible` `a home` MEANS
    Applicant WITH
        `meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)` IS `eligible`
        `the house is to be a home for me and my family` IS `a home`

§§ `For the person buying or building a home`

§§§ `s 15 -- my application`

@export Must the Housing Authority deal with my application (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 15(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am applying for housing or financial help for housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application is for housing or for financial assistance for housing
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Housing Authority deal with my application, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Housing Authority deal with my application` `I am applying for housing or financial help for housing`)
    WHEN `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority` THEN `yes if` (`Must the Housing Authority deal with my application` `I am applying for housing or financial help for housing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35-42 -- a loan from the Housing Authority`

@export Can the Housing Authority lend me money for this purpose (Housing Act 1980 (WA) ss 35-38)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Whether you meet the Authority's eligibility conditions, and whether the house is to be your home
      `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of the loan` @desc What the loan is for
      `the Authority is satisfied my financial position justifies the help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an alteration loan only (s 38(3)): the Authority's judgment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority lend to me for this` `me` `the purpose` `the Authority is satisfied my financial position justifies the help`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Would this new loan keep what I owe the Housing Authority within the Minister's limit (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 40(1), s 73(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `what I owe now under Part IV, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the new loan` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area and purpose` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would this loan keep me within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a Part IV loan` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Would this loan keep me within the Minister's limit` `what I owe now under Part IV, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` `the new loan` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area and purpose`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What security must I give for a Housing Authority loan (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 41(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`What security must I give for a Part IV loan, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a Part IV loan` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` `What security must I give for a Part IV loan`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What interest rate will my Housing Authority loan or contract of sale on terms carry (Housing Act 1980 (WA) ss 33(6), 42(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `the standard rate most recently gazetted for this class` IS A NUMBER @desc Percent a year (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A `Rate`
`What interest rate will I pay, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `I owe the Authority nothing for it` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `percent a year` (`What interest rate will I pay` `the standard rate most recently gazetted for this class`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 46, 47 -- help with a loan from another lender`

@export Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing to build, finish or buy a new home (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Whether you meet the Authority's eligibility conditions, and whether the house is to be your home
      `I want to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 46(1)(a)-(c)
      `I can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Your deposit
      `I cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether lenders will lend you the rest unaided
      `the value of the house, not counting the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a loan from another lender` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing` `me` `I want to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house` `I can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves` `I cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee` `the value of the house, not counting the land` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my home loan (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Whether you meet the Authority's eligibility conditions, and whether the house is to be your home
      `the Authority has approved me in writing for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(2) "approved person"
      `my lender is approved in writing by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(2) "approved lending institution"
      `the loan is secured by a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loan is secured by a mortgage of freehold or leasehold property
      `the Minister approves the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(1)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a loan from another lender` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan` `me` `the Authority has approved me in writing for this` `my lender is approved in writing by the Minister` `the loan is secured by a mortgage` `the Minister approves the payments`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What does the Housing Act 1980 (WA) itself decide about my home loan from this lender?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the lender` IS A Lender @desc Who is lending to you
GIVETH A `Text answer`
`What does the Housing Act decide about my loan, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN `the answer is` (`What does the Housing Act decide about my loan from` `the lender`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31-34 -- buying a house or land from the Housing Authority`

@export Can the rent I (or my partner) paid be credited towards buying the house from the Housing Authority (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 31(1)(a), (b)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my rent be credited towards the price I pay the Authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a Division 4 purchase` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can my rent be credited towards the price` TRUE `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me a home (Housing Act 1980 (WA) ss 32, 33(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Whether you meet the Authority's eligibility conditions, and whether the house is to be your home
      `what is for sale` IS A `What the Authority would sell me` @desc What the Authority would sell
GIVETH A `Terms answer`
`On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a Division 4 purchase` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`On what terms can the Housing Authority sell me this` `me` `what is for sale`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Would the unpaid price under my contract with the Housing Authority stay within the Minister's limit (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 34(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `the unpaid balance, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Would the unpaid price stay within the Minister's limit, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `it is not a Division 4 purchase` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Would the unpaid price stay within the Minister's limit` `the unpaid balance, leaving out fees and duty added under s 73` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for this area`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 68, 72, 73 -- paying the Housing Authority`

@export Can the Housing Authority give me more time to pay what I owe it on my loan or purchase (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 68)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
      `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 68
      `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Authority's judgment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be given more time to pay on my loan or purchase` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `I owe the Authority nothing for it` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be given more time to pay the Authority` `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor` `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Housing Authority pay my stamp duty and registration fees and add them to what I owe (Housing Act 1980 (WA) ss 72, 73)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I am buying` IS A `How I am buying` @desc How you are buying or building your home: with a Housing Authority loan, buying from the Housing Authority itself, or with a loan from Keystart, a bank or another lender
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Authority pay my duty and add it to what I owe, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building a home and want the Housing Authority's help` THEN
        IF `I owe the Authority nothing for it` `how I am buying`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the Authority pay my duty and add it to what I owe` TRUE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person who rents, or wants to rent, from the Housing Authority`

§§§ `ss 28, 30 -- renting a house from the Authority`

@export Can the Housing Authority rent me one of its houses (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 28)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc Whether you meet the Authority's eligibility conditions, and whether the house is to be your home
      `the Authority thinks I provide an essential community or tradesman service here and cannot find suitable accommodation elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 28(b): the Authority's opinion
      `the Minister consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 28: needed for a person who is not eligible
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority rent me a house, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority` THEN `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority rent me a house` `me` `the Authority thinks I provide an essential community or tradesman service here and cannot find suitable accommodation elsewhere` `the Minister consents`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much rent must I pay the Housing Authority (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I rent a home from the Housing Authority now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you rent a home from the Housing Authority now
      `the rent determined for my house and my class of tenant` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars a week, from the Authority's determination
      `the rebate the determination allows me` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars a week
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much rent must I pay, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority` THEN
        IF NOT (`I rent a home from the Housing Authority now`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much rent must I pay` `the rent determined for my house and my class of tenant` `the rebate the determination allows me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 31 -- buying the house I rent`

@export If I buy the house I (or my partner) rented from the Housing Authority, can the rent be credited towards the price (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am buying the house and land from the Authority under Division 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 31(1)
      `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 31(1)(a), (b)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my rent be credited towards buying the house I rent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority` THEN `yes if` (`Can my rent be credited towards the price` `I am buying the house and land from the Authority under Division 4` `I, or my spouse or de facto partner (living or dead), rented this house from the Authority`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 60 -- specialised housing`

@export Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing such as student or aged housing (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 60)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Authority thinks my housing needs are not otherwise adequately provided for under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 60(1)(a): the Authority's opinion
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing, as I ask it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority` THEN `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority house me in specialised housing` `the Authority thinks my housing needs are not otherwise adequately provided for under the Act`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 68 -- more time to pay`

@export Can the Housing Authority give me more time to pay my rent or what else I owe it (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 68)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I rent a home from the Housing Authority now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you rent a home from the Housing Authority now
      `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 68
      `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Authority's judgment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be given more time to pay my rent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I rent, or want to rent, a home from the Housing Authority` THEN
        IF NOT (`I rent a home from the Housing Authority now`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be given more time to pay the Authority` `I owe the Authority money as a purchaser, tenant, borrower or other debtor` `the Authority accepts mine is a case of hardship`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a bank or other institution lending to a home buyer`

§§§ `ss 46, 47 -- the Authority's guarantee and interest subsidy`

@export Can the Housing Authority guarantee this home buyer's borrowing from us (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the borrower meets the Authority's eligibility conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the borrower meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)
      `the house is to be the borrower's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the house is to be a home for the borrower and the borrower's family
      `the borrower wants to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 46(1)(a)-(c)
      `the borrower can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The borrower's deposit
      `the borrower cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the borrower could borrow the rest unaided
      `the value of the house, not counting the land` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars
      `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars (not deposited; an input)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority guarantee this borrower's loan from us` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a bank or other institution lending to a home buyer` THEN `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority guarantee my borrowing` (`the borrower as an applicant` `the borrower meets the Authority's eligibility conditions` `the house is to be the borrower's home`) `the borrower wants to build a house, finish a part-built house or buy a new house` `the borrower can pay, without borrowing, the part of the cost the Authority approves` `the borrower cannot borrow the balance without the Authority's guarantee` `the value of the house, not counting the land` `the sum the Minister has gazetted for house values here`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy on our loan to this home buyer (Housing Act 1980 (WA) s 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the borrower meets the Authority's eligibility conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the borrower meets the Authority's eligibility conditions for this kind of help (policy)
      `the Authority has approved the borrower in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(2) "approved person"
      `we are approved in writing by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(2) "approved lending institution"
      `the loan is secured by a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loan is secured by a mortgage of freehold or leasehold property
      `the Minister approves the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 47(1)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Housing Authority pay us an interest subsidy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a bank or other institution lending to a home buyer` THEN `yes if` (`Can the Housing Authority subsidise the interest on my loan` (`the borrower as an applicant` `the borrower meets the Authority's eligibility conditions` TRUE) `the Authority has approved the borrower in writing` `we are approved in writing by the Minister` `the loan is secured by a mortgage` `the Minister approves the payments`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
